     If you ask for 7 candles or less, you'll get the exact
amount you've requested (provided the amount is at least 1,
that is).  When you ask for more (or explicitly request 0
or a negative value), you'll get whatever random amount the
object was created with, same as not specifying any quantity.
For candles, that amount starts at 1, with a 50% chance of
adding a random increase between 0 and 6 (inclusive).  The
odds are approximately 57% chance to get 1, 7% each to get
2, 3, ..., or 7.


